      "directory": "libssc",
      "sha256": "716d6bd6b34d2d753060c6b54c9a87e34fae75b724c763bf9ef487efa3621587",
      "checksum_source": "Debian libssc_0.4.4-2.dsc (Checksums-Sha256); identical bytes to the upstream archive of the same commit",
      "upstream_commit": "0cf77b93b55752da34dca2dcecc06fca8665184b",
      "license": "GPL-3.0-or-later",
      "patches": [
        {
          "file": "patches/libssc/0001-libssc-select-the-delivery-and-batching-of-streams-at-run-time.patch",
          "sha256": "0d9945fcde4de14a42eef92f0ff6d71d92a301a978bcac596bd29b667205db00",
          "origin": "this project",
          "upstream_status": "not submitted",
          "note": "Stream requests take their delivery type and optional batching from SSC_SUSPEND_MODE, SSC_BATCH_PERIOD_US and SSC_FLUSH_PERIOD_US, read once per process; without them the requests are unchanged. Made the single-variable wake-up A/B of the ADSP SMP2P interrupts possible; 0002 turns the unset case into a per-sensor-type default.",
          "evidence": [
            {
              "rom_file": "vendor.img:/lib64/libsnsapi-full.so",
              "sha256": "0ccf31f2189b7d1c109730de6611222b3da7de81d175ad630ddde7d0192fecec",
              "shows": "embedded descriptors: sns_client_request_msg.susp_config (3) = {client_proc_type 1, delivery_type 2 (SNS_CLIENT_DELIVERY_WAKEUP 0, NO_WAKEUP 1), nowakeup_msg_ids 3}; sns_std_request.batching (1) = batch_spec {batch_period 1, flush_period 2, flush_only 3, max_batch 4}, payload 2, is_passive 3"
            },
            {
              "rom_file": "vendor.img:/lib64/sensors.qsh.so",
              "sha256": "60964b6b4a3d812f4e819071e13c99301aed266b09ac37702617c3c50feeaacb",
              "shows": "stock sensor HAL log formats: 'asked batch_period_us', 'convert sample_period=%lu to batch_period=%u', 'bp=%u, fp=%u' and per-sensor _wakeup_type"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "file": "patches/libssc/0002-libssc-choose-the-stream-delivery-by-sensor-type.patch",
          "sha256": "435d75da463a7615c9c7e9b183f68b4eb011be35b0edc56880fc9f73d72770c1",
          "origin": "this project",
          "upstream_status": "not submitted",
          "note": "Without SSC_SUSPEND_MODE the stream request of a sensor takes the delivery of its data type: accel, gyro, mag and rotv non-wakeup (delivery_type 1), every other type wake-up as in 0.4.4; streams stay unbatched unless SSC_BATCH_PERIOD_US is set. SSC_SUSPEND_MODE=wakeup|nowakeup still forces one delivery for every stream of the process (A/B and fallback). On this tablet non-wakeup delivery of the 5 Hz accelerometer stream removed the per-sample ADSP SMP2P interrupts (4.9/s to 0) with the sample rate unchanged; behaviour while the processor is suspended is not measured.",
          "evidence": [
            {
              "url": "https://source.android.com/docs/core/interaction/sensors/suspend-mode",
              "shows": "non-wake-up sensors neither keep the SoC awake nor wake it to report; while it is suspended their events wait in the FIFO and are delivered when it wakes, oldest dropped when full; by type, only proximity and significant motion were wake-up sensors before per-sensor flags"
            },
            {
              "rom_file": "vendor.img:/lib64/sensors.qsh.so",
              "sha256": "60964b6b4a3d812f4e819071e13c99301aed266b09ac37702617c3c50feeaacb",
              "shows": "stock sensor HAL requests the delivery type per sensor (_wakeup_type)"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
